            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 13 changed paths. The change swaps --function-context for -U3 in the guarded git diff args (still --no-ext-diff, --no-textconv, --no-color, and --end-of-options before the commit values), so no new command-injection or external-program surface is introduced.",
              "The new changed-paths line in engine/review/app/launch.go is placed outside the fenced block; changedPaths uses strconv.Quote for any path that Go would escape (newlines, quotes, control characters) or that contains ', ', so a hostile path name cannot start its own line or inject a heading into the reviewer brief. A test in engine/review/app/launch_test.go covers a newline-bearing path, a comma-space path and a quote-bearing path.",
              "Paths are the bound candidate paths, already part of the binding; no secrets or additional data are exposed beyond the diff the reviewer already received. The size limit (review.MaxReplyBytes) check still applies to brief plus context.",
              "Remaining edits are renames (FunctionContextDiff to ContextDiff), docs and tests with no security impact."
            ]
          }
        }
